// logos — the TeX-family logos as macros over the engine's box primitives, for any
// document that wants them. Import this module with:
//
//     \use{logos}
//
// The engine ships only primitives; logos are document-language, like any other
// format-level macro. \LaTeX sets the small A in a \vbox whose height is a measured
// T, with \vss filling beneath, so its apex rides at the cap height (Lamport's own
// construction). \TeXish is this engine's mark — \TeX with a slanted "ish" raised
// against the X. The small letters and the kerns are all relative to the current size
// (\fontscale and em/ex units), so every logo scales cleanly from a footnote to a
// title — the A and the "ish" stay 0.7 of the surrounding letters at any size.
\def TeX {T\kern-.1667em\lower.5ex\hbox{E}\kern-.125em X}
\def LaTeX {L\kern-.36em\setbox latexAbox \hbox{T}\vbox to:\ht latexAbox {\hbox{\fontscale{.7}{regular}A}\vss}\kern-.15em\TeX}
\def TeXish {\TeX\kern-.14em\raise.22em\hbox{\fontscale{.7}{slanted}ish}}
